Regarding that "You aren't sure you're doing this the right way..."
message, =96 I haven't actually played unnethack, so I dont' know
exactly how it works, but it sounds similar to the message in vanilla
that you get when fighting as a monk wearing body armour. (about the
armour being cumbersome).

I found it really annoying seeing that message every single time I
attacked. It's good to be told that the armour is making it hard to
fight, but I don't need to be told _every single hit_.

... Anyway, I've changed it in my own code. In my opinion, the best
way to do it is to only display those kinds of messages when you
actually miss. Eg, if you attack and miss in unnethack because of the
'restricted' hit-chance cap thing, _then_ you should see the message.
If you hit successfully, then no message.


